## Lore

The stage magician is an escape artist and an illusionist who uses no real magic
at all - only misdirection, dexterity, and an intimate knowledge of locks, knots
and hidden pockets. The character has had some formal schooling, if only high
school.

It is worth keeping this one apart from the Magic power category''s Magician,
whose illusions are spells. This character''s are tricks, and that is the point
of him.

## GM Notes

**The illusion and escape list**, printed 159 - eight of the fourteen, with the
one-time bonus the book prints beside each:

Climbing including rappelling (+25%); Concealment (+30%); Detect Concealment
(+30%); Disguise (+30%); Escape Artist (+30%); Forgery (+15%); Impersonation
(+25%); Palming (+30%); Pick Locks (+30%); Pick Pockets (+30%); Prowl (+25%);
Optic Systems (+20%); Surveillance Systems (+5%); T.V./Video (+20%).

**The equipment budget**, printed 160: 01-12 $6,500; 13-24 $7,000; 25-38 $8,200;
39-52 $10,000; 53-65 $12,000; 66-78 $14,000; 79-90 $16,000; 91-00 $18,000. At
least 50% must go on tools and items usable for tricks and feats of magic - a
couple of sets of lock picks and night optics are a must - and another 20% on
other crimefighting items; up to 30% may be saved. The character presumably has
a furnished apartment and an 86% chance of a sports car, 1D6 years old.

**Special gimmicks**, printed 160, begin with tailor-made clothing carrying
secret pockets and seams for concealment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
